## Spec docs/specs/stdlib/task_spawn.spec.md §B1 / §B3 / §B4 e2e.
##
## Two CountdownFutures spawned via `Task.spawn_raw`, then each
## joined via `Task.join(h).await`. The driver suspends back through
## `block_on`'s outer pump loop on every await, so the spawned tasks
## advance round-robin against the scheduler queue without any
## hand-pumping inside the driver.
##
## This is the post-Gap-1, post-Gap-2 shape — what the original
## hand-pump variant was deferring until the v1 missing-features
## work landed:
##   * Gap 1 (commit f899788): `Task.spawn_raw(fut)` is now
##     recognised as a move-by-FFI handoff by drop elaboration —
##     the local `f1` / `f2` bindings DON'T get a scope-exit drop
##     emitted that would `riven_dealloc` the heap block out from
##     under the scheduler.
##   * Gap 2 (commit 7fc8a1e + 447e280): the Milestone-2B segmenter
##     accepts pre-await statements (`let f1 = ...; let h1 =
##     Task.spawn_raw(f1)`) before the first `.await`, and the
##     MIR class-name parser for synth state-machine classes
##     emits the correct class_info_ptr header shift so outer
##     args read back correctly inside `init`.
##
## What this proves end-to-end:
##   - Task.spawn_raw enqueues a future without polling it.
##   - The block_on inline loop's pump call drives every queued
##     task forward in round-robin order (no starvation), even
##     across multiple `.await` suspends in the driver.
##   - Task.join(handle).await yields the i64 payload after the
##     spawned task transitions to Ready.
##   - Two tasks completing both their N-step countdowns sum
##     correctly: 11 + 22 == 33.

class CountdownFuture
  remaining: Int
  payload: Int
  include Future
  type Output = Int

  def init(n: Int, p: Int)
    self.remaining = n
    self.payload = p
  end

  def var poll(cx: &var Context) -> Poll[Int]
    if self.remaining == 0
      Poll.Ready(self.payload)
    else
      self.remaining = self.remaining - 1
      Poll.Pending
    end
  end
end

## Driver: spawn two countdowns, chain `Task.join(h).await` on both,
## return their sum. Both spawn locals live in the pre-await prefix
## (Gap 2 segmenter); the move-by-FFI handoff (Gap 1) keeps drop
## elaboration from freeing the spawned futures while the scheduler
## still owns them.
async def driver -> Int
  let f1 = CountdownFuture.new(3, 11)
  let f2 = CountdownFuture.new(5, 22)
  let h1 = Task.spawn_raw(f1)
  let h2 = Task.spawn_raw(f2)
  let v1 = Task.join(h1).await
  let v2 = Task.join(h2).await
  v1 + v2
end

def main
  let total = block_on(driver())
  if total == 33
    puts "ok"
  else
    puts "fail"
  end
end
